i think nethack 3.1 will feature many new things but it is on hold until
version 3.0 is nearly bug-free. also, there may be other sites but you can get
the latest version of nethack in "tar"red, "compress"ed, "uuencode"d format
from /pub/NH3.0 at linc.cis.upenn.edu. that version includes patchlevel4 but
is missing the stopgap shops patch and features a make-dependency loop that
may or may not be a problem for your compiler.

there have been lot's of great ideas that have been posted here that i hope
make it into v3.1. how about some more monsters (ohh nooo ...)?
A - hairy Automaton - mechanical ape, neutral, appears early, carries keys.
c - common cold - it coughs, you feel a chill, gives cold resistance.
e - floating exception - non-aggresive, if struck with a non-blessed weapon
        it simply multiplies itself by the number equal to your luck.
        generally gets in the way. may be kicked or bare-handed effectively.
f - lion cub - a young lion, nothing special.
f - lion - very nasty, when eaten, randomly adds to St or Dx or Co.
g - griffin - a rogue nasty, perhaps a super gremlin.
L - leper - steals gold a/o gems. can induce vomiting or stun you.
q - jabberwock (sp?) - another rogue nasty.
Q - earth quaker - doesn't hit for damage but on occasion creates a pit
        where you are standing. a handy place for unused boulders.
x - xanthic nail - unlike xans, this guy will occasionally pierce your boots.
        carries a nail which can be applied to traps making them ineffective.
        i.e. you can now nail the trapdoor shut.

i know there's got to be others so let's hear about 'em!!!

